  "source": "one-continuous-master",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "line-01",
      "text": "Once released from prison, Pinocchio hurried back toward the Blue Fairy.",
      "start": 0.138,
      "end": 5.11
    },
    {
      "id": "line-02",
      "text": "A giant smoking Serpent blocked the road and frightened him senseless.",
      "start": 5.11,
      "end": 12.532
    },
    {
      "id": "line-03",
      "text": "Later, hunger tempted Pinocchio to steal grapes from a vineyard.",
      "start": 12.532,
      "end": 16.756
    },
    {
      "id": "line-04",
      "text": "A hidden trap snapped shut and held both wooden legs.",
      "start": 16.756,
      "end": 22.189
    },
    {
      "id": "line-05",
      "text": "The farmer who found him chained the puppet beside his chicken coop.",
      "start": 22.189,
      "end": 27.101
    },
    {
      "id": "line-06",
      "text": "Pinocchio was ordered to replace Melampo, the farmer's dead watchdog.",
      "start": 27.101,
      "end": 33.559
    },
    {
      "id": "line-07",
      "text": "That night, Weasels offered him food for allowing their usual theft.",
      "start": 33.559,
      "end": 39.384
    },
    {
      "id": "line-08",
      "text": "Instead of accepting the bargain, Pinocchio trapped them and alerted the farmer.",
      "start": 39.384,
      "end": 46.034
    },
    {
      "id": "line-09",
      "text": "Impressed by this unexpected honesty, the farmer removed the humiliating collar.",
      "start": 46.034,
      "end": 53.13
    },
    {
      "id": "line-10",
      "text": "At the Fairy's home, Pinocchio discovered a stone claiming she had died.",
      "start": 53.13,
      "end": 59.677
    },
    {
      "id": "line-11",
      "text": "His grief continued until a great Pigeon brought news of Geppetto.",
      "start": 59.677,
      "end": 65.505
    },
    {
      "id": "line-12",
      "text": "The bird explained that his father had built a small boat to search overseas.",
      "start": 65.505,
      "end": 71.528
    },
    {
      "id": "line-13",
      "text": "Pinocchio climbed onto the Pigeon's back without hesitating.",
      "start": 71.528,
      "end": 75.878
    },
    {
      "id": "line-14",
      "text": "They flew through the entire night and reached the coast by morning.",
      "start": 75.878,
      "end": 81.726
    },
    {
      "id": "line-15",
      "text": "Offshore, Pinocchio recognized Geppetto struggling as a storm overturned the boat.",
      "start": 81.726,
      "end": 88.99
    },
    {
      "id": "line-16",
      "text": "He threw himself into the rough sea, determined to reach his father.",
      "start": 88.99,
      "end": 94.65
    }
  ],
